# Beat The Scam — Local environment variables
# =============================================
# 1. Copy this file:   cp .env.example .env
# 2. Fill in your real keys (see comments below)
# 3. NEVER commit .env to git (it's already in .gitignore)

# ── Twitter API (used by scripts that auto-tweet new guides) ──────────────
# From your Twitter App → Keys and Tokens
TWITTER_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
TWITTER_API_KEY_SECRET=your_api_key_secret_here
TWITTER_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_access_token_here
TWITTER_ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET=your_access_token_secret_here

# ── Netlify Function env (set in the Netlify dashboard, NOT used by local
#    build/content scripts; only needed locally if you run `netlify dev`) ───
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY      — AI scam checker (check-scam.js). The checker also uses
#                          Netlify Blobs (auto-provisioned, no secret) for an
#                          atomic (compare-and-set) per-IP rate limit + daily
#                          spend cap. IP keys are stored HASHED, never raw.
# RESEND_API_KEY         — newsletter (double opt-in); must be a FULL-ACCESS key
# RESEND_AUDIENCE_ID     — target Resend Audience id (Audiences → </> snippet)
# UNSUBSCRIBE_SECRET     — HMAC key for BOTH the one-click unsubscribe links AND
#                          the double opt-in confirm links; `openssl rand -hex 32`.
#                          NOW REQUIRED FOR SIGNUP: if unset, subscribe.js returns
#                          500 (fails closed — never mints a forgeable token).
# RATE_LIMIT_SALT        — OPTIONAL salt for hashing the IP/email rate-limit keys
#                          in check-scam.js + subscribe.js, so raw IPs/addresses
#                          are never persisted in Blobs. `openssl rand -hex 16`.
#                          Falls back to a built-in constant if unset (still
#                          hashes; set it for a stronger per-deploy secret).
#
# subscribe.js also uses Netlify Blobs (auto-provisioned) for a durable per-
# address daily cap + global send cap, and confirm-subscribe.js uses it to make
# confirm links single-use. No secret needed for those stores.
#
# Netlify Functions carry a package.json (@netlify/blobs); deps are installed by
# Netlify's function bundler, not the Python build.

# ── Content pipeline / CI-only secrets (GitHub Actions secrets, not usually
#    needed locally — documented here for the full inventory) ───────────────
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY            — also needed LOCALLY if you run the content
#                                scripts (run_daily_publish.py,
#                                generate_content_claude.py, content_gate.py,
#                                gate_selftest.py, audit_corpus.py).
# GOOGLE_SEARCH_CONSOLE_TOKEN  — daily-search-console.yml + auth_google.py /
#                                search_console_articles.py / gsc_report.py.
#                                ⚠️ rots ~weekly; re-auth via scripts/auth_google.py.
# DIGEST_TO                    — weekly-audit.yml / audit_digest.py: recipient
#                                for the weekly editorial-audit digest email.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your_key_here
# GOOGLE_SEARCH_CONSOLE_TOKEN=your_oauth_token_json_here
# DIGEST_TO=you@example.com

